# NoDitto — Android release configuration (template).
#
# Copy this file to `config/prod.env`, fill in real values, and build with:
#   flutter build appbundle --release --dart-define-from-file=config/prod.env
#
# `config/prod.env` is git-ignored (Req 6.6). THIS file is tracked, so it must
# never hold a real value. Every value below is a placeholder.
#
# Nothing here may be a service-role key or a Stripe secret key (Req 6.4). This
# file is compiled into an app bundle that ships to devices, so anything the app
# can read is disclosed. Every key below is publishable or public by design.
#
# The four keys marked REQUIRED are the Required_Config_Keys checked at startup
# by `lib/core/config_gate.dart`. Under a release build a missing or malformed
# one is fatal: the app shows a configuration-failure screen naming the key and
# no member surface (Req 6.2). Under debug it is reported and the app continues
# (Req 6.3). Strictness comes from `kReleaseMode` — see PRODUCTION below.

# REQUIRED. Supabase project URL.
# Rule: non-empty after trimming, and an absolute https URL with a host.
# Shape only — do not commit a real project ref to this template.
SUPABASE_URL=https://<project>.supabase.co

# REQUIRED. Supabase anonymous (publishable) key.
# Rule: non-empty after trimming.
# This is the ANON key. The service-role key bypasses RLS and must never appear
# in a client build, in this file, or in `config/prod.env`.
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<anon-key>

# REQUIRED. Stripe publishable key.
# Rule: non-empty after trimming AND prefixed `pk_`. A secret (`sk_`),
# restricted (`rk_`) or webhook-signing (`whsec_`) value fails the prefix test
# and is reported as MISSING rather than accepted (Req 6.5) — a secret key in a
# shipped bundle should be loud, not quietly functional.
STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_live_PLACEHOLDER

# REQUIRED. Base URL of the deployed web app.
# Rule: non-empty after trimming, and an absolute https URL with a host.
# This is both the handoff target (identity verification, payout setup) and the
# origin of every mobile API call, because `ApiRoutes.base` is
# `WEB_APP_URL + /api/mobile`.
#
# Unlike the Supabase keys, this one keeps a baked-in default in
# `lib/core/env.dart` — the production origin below. So omitting it does not
# fail the gate; it falls back to the same value. Set it anyway: the fallback is
# a stale-host hazard the day the origin changes, and the gate does still reject
# a malformed override here (missing scheme, plain http, embedded whitespace).
# The reasoning for the inconsistency with D5 is recorded on the field itself.
WEB_APP_URL=https://noditto.app

# Optional. Default browse region when nothing else resolves.
# Defaults to `AU` in `lib/core/env.dart`; not checked by the config gate.
# This is a BROWSE default only. It never becomes anyone's trading region.
DEFAULT_REGION=AU

# Optional. Names the environment. Defaults to false.
#
# PRODUCTION DOES NOT CONTROL STRICTNESS. This is the single most likely
# misreading of this file. The fail-closed gate keys off `kReleaseMode`, a build
# fact, precisely because `PRODUCTION` is itself a config value: gating
# strictness on it would mean a typo here (`PRODUCTION=flase`) ships a release
# in permissive mode. See design decision D4. Setting it false in a release
# build changes no validation and disables no check.
PRODUCTION=true

# Optional. DSN for the error reporter.
#
# Empty (the default, and the current state) is valid: no provider has been
# chosen, so the seam in `lib/core/observability/error_reporter.dart` binds a
# reporter that writes to the device log and SENDS NOTHING OFF THE DEVICE. See
# design decision D13. Because nothing leaves the device, leaving this unset is
# not a Play Data safety obligation today.
#
# Setting it changes that: errors would then be transmitted to a third party,
# which needs a matching diagnostic-data declaration in the Data safety form
# before the build ships. A DSN is an ingestion endpoint, not a secret — it is
# designed to ship inside client bundles — but it is still optional rather than
# required, because a build with no reporter configured must run.
ERROR_REPORTER_DSN=
